      11 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِرْبَاثَّ</span></b> , (K, TA,) or ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِرْبَأَثَّ</span></b> , (CK,) <i>He was,</i>
or <i>became, hindered, withheld, restrained,</i> or <i>debarred.</i> (K, TA.) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَنَا فُلَانٌ ثُمَّ ٱرْبَاثَّ</span>
<i>Such a one drew near,</i> or <i>approached: then
became hindered, withheld,</i> &amp;c. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See
also 9.

